 # Beam Tracing
-
 ## Overview
-Beam tracing is an acceleration technique for ray tracing that represents a "thick" ray as a pyramid (or cone) to shoot several rays at once, creating new beams at polygon surfaces [S1, unofficial]. It is a strategy where rays are considered only in a final sampling step, rather than being represented explicitly during traversal [S2]. It is competitive with frustum-based tracers for eye and shadow rays [S2].
