 ## How it works
-Beam tracing accelerates light transport by aggregating rays into geometric volumes (beams) rather than processing them individually.
-
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Input:** A scene defined by polygonal surfaces and a set of primary rays (e.g., eye rays or shadow rays).
-*   **Output:** A set of sampled rays or final pixel values derived from the beam intersections.
