 ## Background
-Beam tracing was introduced as an acceleration technique in computer graphics to handle ray tracing efficiency [S1, unofficial]. It is discussed in the context of bounding volumes and acceleration data structures [S1, unofficial]. Overbeck et al. demonstrated its competitiveness with frustum-based tracers [S2]. The method is part of the broader category of real-time approximations for light transport in participating media [Parent].
